dsv41 patch 0066 (21.10.2026): the DSpark drafter cheaper per verify round, three switches. VLLM_DSV41_MARKOV_FUSED=1
in use (with 0067, image v18 and later); VLLM_DSV41_MARKOV_TRIM off (-0.42 % per round alone, +0.04 % on top of
MARKOV_FUSED); VLLM_DSV41_DRAFT_L2PF off (-0.01 %). Base: the v12 files; no file of 0064 or 0065 is touched.
Why: the drafter pass costs ~3.6 ms a round at 1 stream (profile of 19.10., 192 kernels), ~0.52 ms of it the Markov
loop: five sequential steps of ~13 small kernels each (torch.max over the 64,640-column shard alone ~15 us), 46-53 us
a step with a cached bias row, ~186 us with a computed one. The loop always runs 5 steps although the 0047 window
verifies 2-3 drafts at prose. And the drafter's dense weights are never prefetched into L2 (its modules are outside
l2pf.py's chain), while TensorFold's batched drafter graph forks paced L2 prefetches per stage.
How:
  1. VLLM_DSV41_MARKOV_FUSED=1 (new nvidia/ops/markov_step.py; dspark.py; dspark speculator): each greedy local-argmax
     step as the unchanged bias kernel -> a reduction kernel (base + bias rounded to bf16 as torch's add rounds it, per
     2,048 columns the maximum and its first column in torch.max's order: NaN above all, -0.0 = +0.0, ties to the
     lower index) -> one all-gather of the chunk maxima -> a pick kernel (the first maximum over rank and chunk; writes
     the draft, the next step's previous token and its Markov embedding). Three kernels and one all-gather a step
     instead of ~13 kernels; the same drafts bit for bit.
  2. VLLM_DSV41_MARKOV_TRIM=1 (gpu_worker.py, dflash and dspark speculators): the scheduler's draft count for the next
     step (dynamic schedule + 0047 window) reaches the speculator before each step; under async scheduling no request
     verifies more drafts than that. A FULL graph holds a fixed loop, so the DSpark graphs are captured once more for
     each shorter depth (VLLM_DSV41_AK_MIN .. k-1) and replayed by depth; the 12 never-dispatched DSpark graphs of the
     0047 widths are dropped, so the graph count stays at 16. Confidences past the depth are 0.
  3. VLLM_DSV41_DRAFT_L2PF=next[,attn] (new vllm_exl3_moe/l2pf_draft.py; dense.py, config.py, moe_method.py, dspark.py):
     a second prefetch chain over the three drafter blocks with l2pf.py's kernel and pacing. "next" after block j's MoE
     pulls block j+1's mHC mix (EXL3_L2PF_HC=1), wq_a+wkv and wq_b; "attn" after wq_b pulls wo_a and wo_b. The chain is
     joined before the drafter graph ends, so it never overlaps the target's MoE reads (0063's slowdown). Drafter passes
     above EXL3_DRAFT_L2PF_MAX_ROWS (16) rows prefetch nothing.
Bits: 1 changes no draft; 2 changes no verified draft, only the depth choice in rounds where the policy wanted more
drafts than the window has; 3 writes nothing. The target's verification decides every emitted token, so T=0 texts stay
the same with all three. Tested on CPU (the kernel sources on an interpreter against the original step) and on GB10
(8/8 bit-identical).
Measured (21.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz, image v18 = v12 + 0064 + 0066 + 0067, three arms one after the other, each from a
fresh start against the stored reference run of the production setup with 0064 and the CPU pin; prose / code / JSON at
1 and 4 streams, T = 0 and 1, plus 64K cells):
  MARKOV_FUSED + 0067's VOR_FUSED   cost per verify round -0.66 % (geometric mean, worst cell +1.5 %), tok/s -0.78 %,
                                    T=0 identical; the tok/s loss is the code cell at 64K context (-18.5 % at -3.3 % ms
                                    per round: T=0 texts are not reproducible at 64K, so it compares two texts)
  MARKOV_TRIM alone                 -0.42 % (worst cell +0.1 %), tok/s -0.42 % (64K cells -5.7 / -2.9 %), T=0 identical
  DRAFT_L2PF=next alone             -0.01 %, tok/s +0.24 %, T=0 identical
  MARKOV_TRIM on top of the first   +0.04 % (worst cell +3.7 %), tok/s +2.32 % (other texts), T=0 identical; measured
  row (later, on image v20)         against the stored run of the first row: not adopted
All three with 0067 in an earlier window against the same reference: +1.32 % per round (1-stream cells +1.7..+2.6 %),
tok/s -0.40 %, T=0 identical. Each switch alone measured <= 0; what slowed the combination down is not resolved.
Switches: VLLM_DSV41_MARKOV_FUSED=1; VLLM_DSV41_MARKOV_TRIM=1 (or a comma list of depths); VLLM_DSV41_DRAFT_L2PF=next or
attn,next (EXL3_DRAFT_L2PF_MAX_ROWS; budget / pacing / delay as for l2pf.py: EXL3_L2PF_MB / _RATE_GBPS / _DELAY_NS).
All off by default (markov_step.py is then not imported, l2pf_draft.py only reads its switch). FUSED and TRIM need the
greedy local-argmax loop (VLLM_DSPARK_LOCAL_ARGMAX=1, the launcher's default), TRIM also async scheduling; otherwise
they log a warning and stay off.

